WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.016 --> 00:00:11.145
SRS-first onboarding — Sign up, upload a requirements document and let Claude create and pre-fill the project — then complete it in the wizard and generate the WBS.

2
00:00:11.145 --> 00:00:15.463
Create an account — each user only sees their own projects.

3
00:00:15.463 --> 00:00:23.262
The first screen after login: upload the SRS (.pdf, .txt or .md, up to 10 MB).

4
00:00:23.262 --> 00:00:27.657
The Project Key defaults to the file name — rename it if you like.

5
00:00:27.657 --> 00:00:33.835
Claude reads the document and extracts requirements, design and project-setup data… (wait shortened)

6
00:00:34.957 --> 00:00:41.682
Review: what Claude found — requirements, use cases, components and API endpoints.

7
00:00:41.682 --> 00:00:45.868
Open the New Project wizard — pre-filled from the SRS.

8
00:00:45.868 --> 00:00:53.404
Create Project: key, FP estimate, technology, description and scope all came from the SRS.

9
00:00:53.404 --> 00:00:56.895
The start date isn’t in the SRS — add it.

10
00:00:56.895 --> 00:01:02.127
Application Details — name, domain, category and description extracted.

11
00:01:02.127 --> 00:01:06.031
Hardware and software are read from the document…

12
00:01:06.031 --> 00:01:10.556
Risks, constraints, assumptions and dependencies too.

13
00:01:10.556 --> 00:01:14.307
Functional modules identified by Claude.

14
00:01:14.307 --> 00:01:22.078
An SRS never names the team, so a standard role-wise team is added with placeholder people. Assign real ones:

15
00:01:22.078 --> 00:01:28.687
Add what an SRS can’t know: the Kick-Off agenda, process planning and key decisions.

16
00:01:35.007 --> 00:01:39.427
Save Project — the wizard updates the same project in place.

17
00:01:39.427 --> 00:01:45.210
The project home: a Messages section lists what is still missing, each with a fix button.

18
00:01:45.210 --> 00:01:51.978
Before generating, resource loading is checked: each person’s WBS hours against their working time.

19
00:01:51.978 --> 00:01:58.987
A JIRA-ready WBS: tasks per person with dates and estimates — download as Excel or CSV.

20
00:01:58.987 --> 00:02:04.306
The Analysis and Design documents were written by Claude from the SRS.

21
00:02:06.561 --> 00:02:17.284
Done: from SRS to WBS — Project created from the requirements document, completed in the wizard, team assigned and WBS generated.
